{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:48:51.739618Z","id":"e166f16abc3286de3243574eb23d6908bf1c2e7c2fbb420db9e62c6a2bab15de","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs:414-425, record 28025fcc; anchored on RealClients::run_pi's node_modules check, where the replies place the code it is about.\n\nRealClients::pi runs tests/fixtures/pi-agent.mjs with `node --import jiti/register` from plugins/pi, the loader Pi itself uses for extensions (Node's own type stripping rejects clax.ts's parameter properties). every_real_client_runs_against_the_test_daemon fails where node or plugins/pi/node_modules is missing.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:b49f68705d01835492d1dac280996c4007bb4b2d","span":{"start":{"line":452},"end":{"line":458},"content_hash":"491d9994417da8e7f1c0acbdb85fa3b4187b3440755b5b29fd6524f3ddd162a7"},"suggested_fix":"Skip the Pi channel with a message when node_modules is absent, or make sure plugins/pi's node_modules is installed before the Rust tests run.","summary":"The real-client tests need node and plugins/pi/node_modules (jiti)","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:48:51.739699Z","id":"62a2827da48cd9f500644e20e3b4c9baf629b89d19c537d41efd2cce9c6e3499","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/tests/fixtures/pi-agent.mjs, record e3918e09, a file commit bccc4357 deleted; anchored on RealClients::run_pi, which drives the real Pi (`pi --mode rpc`) in its place.\n\nThe driver fakes ExtensionAPI (on, registerTool, registerCommand, sendUserMessage) and emits only session_start, tool_result and session_shutdown; the inject tier's followUp messages are captured only if one arrives before shutdown. Drift between this fake and Pi's real API would go unseen. Kept for now: plan Task 19 replaces it with the real Pi (pi --mode rpc) in RealClients::pi when it un-ignores no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:b49f68705d01835492d1dac280996c4007bb4b2d","span":{"start":{"line":445},"end":{"line":458},"content_hash":"46791dc23e53dffc64fdb19f90617494539305da97a5bdacf5860c7b932f4f38"},"suggested_fix":"Drive `pi --mode rpc` with the extension when Pi is installed (skip with a reason otherwise), or assert the inject loop delivered at least one message.","summary":"Pi's channel is a hand-written host for the extension, not Pi","tags":["review","task-6","revisit:Task 19 un-ignores no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:49:08.948485Z","id":"dba7c97202e33144dbff077917e11d6b046190f7d383f62c7b00d97b6454f0d8","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e166f16abc3286de3243574eb23d6908bf1c2e7c2fbb420db9e62c6a2bab15de","summary":"RealClients::run_pi (9be93c11) now runs the real Pi from plugins/pi/node_modules/@mariozechner/pi-coding-agent/dist/cli.js and panics with 'run `npm ci` in plugins/pi' when it is missing, so a missing install fails loudly rather than skipping. Whether the Rust gates should install it first (scripts/quality_gates.sh runs the pi lane separately) is still open.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:49:08.948574Z","id":"9634b96881401b9a37947a23b701e7f4fcfc98f1433c8e00bd695893eac3e19b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e166f16abc3286de3243574eb23d6908bf1c2e7c2fbb420db9e62c6a2bab15de","summary":"This record's span (clients.rs:414:425) drifted when 9be93c11 rewrote RealClients::pi; it should be re-anchored to run_pi's node_modules check (clients.rs:504-509)","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:49:08.948634Z","id":"6c116498df7c591c4c19cca4873d8679ca6854911f6b0f90feffb70d534ddc06","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e166f16abc3286de3243574eb23d6908bf1c2e7c2fbb420db9e62c6a2bab15de","summary":"The code this record is about is now RealClients::run_pi's check at crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs:505:510 (plugins/pi/node_modules/@mariozechner/pi-coding-agent/dist/cli.js must exist).","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:49:08.948694Z","id":"bbca05a0328eaf661023da54605c89e070b0720dd2aa725859fd8fae689603d9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e166f16abc3286de3243574eb23d6908bf1c2e7c2fbb420db9e62c6a2bab15de","summary":"Under Bazel (af337df1) the real-Pi tests get Node from the pinned toolchain (CLAX_TEST_NODE, $(rootpath @nodejs//:node_bin)) and Pi's packages from //plugins/pi:node_modules as declared test data (crates/clax-server/BUILD.bazel), so they never depend on a local install: scripts/bazel-test.sh --rust passed //crates/clax-server:integration. The native gates still install plugins/pi first (scripts/quality_gates.sh lane_pi, scripts/pnpm-install-stamped.sh plugins/pi). Leaving the close to the owner.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T13:02:56.648574Z","id":"8477ffef52d3d91188f4d65cf842e0f3bc78c1f6dcd21c310851907edfd7e361","body":{"detail":"The record describes the hand-written ExtensionAPI host (crates/clax-server/tests/fixtures/pi-agent.mjs), which commit bccc4357 deleted. Its span, crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs:445:458, is RealClients::run_pi: it starts plugins/pi's node_modules/@mariozechner/pi-coding-agent/dist/cli.js in RPC mode and drives the real Pi, which is what the record's last sentence planned. Nothing in the testkit fakes Pi's ExtensionAPI any more. Owner: close this concern with reason:obsolete, or keep it for a remaining gap?","kind":"comment","references":"62a2827da48cd9f500644e20e3b4c9baf629b89d19c537d41efd2cce9c6e3499","summary":"The concern's fake is gone: these lines are RealClients::run_pi, which runs the real Pi; close it as obsolete?","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:52:33.723334Z","id":"3db512ebaf7a87c26393209d05627b4519d3daf8b6f5b95d30fe57361a5b1927","body":{"detail":"LIMIT (crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs:23) bounds each real client run (line 107) and the Pi conversation (line 561-563). Under a load average near 99, api_canary::no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi, no_canary_reaches_a_persons_agent_through_pi_in_remote_mode and every_real_client_runs_against_the_test_daemon all panicked with 'pi did not finish within 30s' after Pi had answered most of its tool calls; //crates/clax-server:integration__5 rerun alone passed in 11.3 s. AGENTS.md asks for no wall-clock budgets in checks.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":23},"content_hash":"2ced07ebdc74420abef83213cf2976e3c309290e5da62df657277f6ba9d9f711"},"suggested_fix":"Wait on the client's own end (process exit, agent_end) with only Bazel's test timeout as the backstop, or make LIMIT a hang detector far above any loaded run (several minutes) and say so in its doc.","summary":"RealClients' 30 s LIMIT is a wall-clock budget on real client runs, and the Pi canary tests fail at it under load","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:48:33.984014Z","id":"0237ff3d1dba04d64d64fe01415c7bbc1247924b2abe8bdebab93b125474614b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:abba16c8f","summary":"LIMIT is now clax_testkit::HANG (120 s), a hang guard documented as such in crates/clax-testkit/src/lib.rs, and the exits after it use it too. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/... passed (31 of 31 targets) with it.","supersedes":"3db512ebaf7a87c26393209d05627b4519d3daf8b6f5b95d30fe57361a5b1927","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:49:15.163597Z","id":"98db9316a36a1b064763246e48605dacd597a8ee1562f50007a26383963d39e7","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/tests/fixtures/pi-agent.mjs, record e3918e09, a file commit bccc4357 deleted; anchored on RealClients::run_pi, which drives the real Pi (`pi --mode rpc`) in its place.\n\nThe driver fakes ExtensionAPI (on, registerTool, registerCommand, sendUserMessage) and emits only session_start, tool_result and session_shutdown; the inject tier's followUp messages are captured only if one arrives before shutdown. Drift between this fake and Pi's real API would go unseen. Kept for now: plan Task 19 replaces it with the real Pi (pi --mode rpc) in RealClients::pi when it un-ignores no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:b49f68705d01835492d1dac280996c4007bb4b2d","span":{"start":{"line":446},"end":{"line":459},"content_hash":"46791dc23e53dffc64fdb19f90617494539305da97a5bdacf5860c7b932f4f38"},"suggested_fix":"Drive `pi --mode rpc` with the extension when Pi is installed (skip with a reason otherwise), or assert the inject loop delivered at least one message.","summary":"Pi's channel is a hand-written host for the extension, not Pi","supersedes":"62a2827da48cd9f500644e20e3b4c9baf629b89d19c537d41efd2cce9c6e3499","tags":["review","task-6","revisit:Task 19 un-ignores no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:49:15.815532Z","id":"71410688ad1bc99da4b050d4718536f0d83264448ea8a1b5f419c9395be8af3a","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs:414-425, record 28025fcc; anchored on RealClients::run_pi's node_modules check, where the replies place the code it is about.\n\nRealClients::pi runs tests/fixtures/pi-agent.mjs with `node --import jiti/register` from plugins/pi, the loader Pi itself uses for extensions (Node's own type stripping rejects clax.ts's parameter properties). every_real_client_runs_against_the_test_daemon fails where node or plugins/pi/node_modules is missing.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:b49f68705d01835492d1dac280996c4007bb4b2d","span":{"start":{"line":453},"end":{"line":459},"content_hash":"491d9994417da8e7f1c0acbdb85fa3b4187b3440755b5b29fd6524f3ddd162a7"},"suggested_fix":"Skip the Pi channel with a message when node_modules is absent, or make sure plugins/pi's node_modules is installed before the Rust tests run.","summary":"The real-client tests need node and plugins/pi/node_modules (jiti)","supersedes":"e166f16abc3286de3243574eb23d6908bf1c2e7c2fbb420db9e62c6a2bab15de","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:17:45.841072Z","id":"1f35f22156cea01ee17734b66eb11beaded7ac683e01e184319d3277d37d4b10","body":{"detail":"TestServer::get, create_thread, thread, send_thread and events, and helpers in crates/clax-server/tests (api_stream as_browser, api_room try_connect, shell_boot page, api_docs Who::Nobody, and the requests that now carry TestServer::local_browser's cookie), send a viewer cookie a local daemon minted, since a request with no credential at all is refused 401 before any route (covered by crates/clax-server/tests/api_local_trust.rs). Such a viewer differs from the anonymous caller of before only in being a row with its own attention and a resolve naming it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1288},"end":{"line":1296},"content_hash":"15afc160bf1e9e4b4a3dc0b064f33e3076a16e51f0ae3da82db7cf8dd727187b"},"summary":"Tests that spoke as an anonymous loopback browser now speak as an unnamed viewer minted for this machine","tags":["tests","local-trust","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:25:49.588535Z","id":"032d185c8a71457c77eda982b230561db03c91ddaa620d1c4ddd7b97b6032b9d","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-http/src/state.rs:387-460 (AppState::assemble) is the one constructor of the daemon's state, but crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs:734-800 writes the struct literal again with the same values for most fields. This branch added owner_sessions, proc_root, discovery and remote_drivers to both (state.rs:390, 437, 447-448; server.rs:728 and 776-785), and the test copy can silently diverge from production (for example ext_creds uses load_with(clock) here and load there).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":734},"end":{"line":800},"content_hash":"17f840631861fe11b8d8d9bf008771c8e2715420c30cb997507a324dff379ef8"},"suggested_fix":"Build the test state with AppState::assemble(StateParts { … }) and then overwrite the test-specific fields (bot with a fixed KEK, seats limits, sample, question_sleeper, net), so only real differences live in clax-testkit.","summary":"TestServer builds AppState field by field beside AppState::assemble, so each new state field is added twice","tags":["review","review:ri-quality","duplication","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:30:17.464487Z","id":"e5ec1f8750c56ec4eb18b89066b4c3d112a6c4ab0966326f3bf5d281aa6c8d79","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-http/src/state.rs:387-470 AppState::assemble(StateParts) (pub struct StateParts at :344) and crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs:722-810 build the same struct field by field with mostly equal values (wrap_cache, timeouts, working/drafts/presence/rooms/live_layers on the clock, stream, discovery, remote_drivers, call_ids, agent_gate). The real differences (bot KEK, seats limits, sample, net, ext_creds via load_with(clock), lan_host, test_daemon, question_sleeper, shutdown) can be overwritten after assemble, so the fix works; ext_creds would be loaded twice unless StateParts takes the clock for it.","kind":"comment","references":"032d185c8a71457c77eda982b230561db03c91ddaa620d1c4ddd7b97b6032b9d","summary":"confirmed: TestServer writes AppState's literal beside AppState::assemble","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T06:40:52.957449Z","id":"0238aff7d486a9d5550f39a89e7473955bcb7c7b69468ac52045e276a102c4bd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:adc2294c9","summary":"TestServer::start builds its state with AppState::assemble(StateParts { ... }) and overwrites only bot (fixed KEK), seats (default limits), lan_host and test_daemon; assemble loads extension credentials with load_with(&store, parts.clock), the system clock on the daemon and the Worker. bazel test //crates/... passes (61 targets).","supersedes":"032d185c8a71457c77eda982b230561db03c91ddaa620d1c4ddd7b97b6032b9d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T19:14:51.929489Z","id":"d27c2237040e1375cc0f966d5f37b0e8e210d87291a59aea35fb519b09ee75c5","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0238aff7d486a9d5550f39a89e7473955bcb7c7b69468ac52045e276a102c4bd","summary":"Commit adc2294c9 cited by this close was re-signed as da5fbc412 (same tree, author and message).","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
